You are running Stage C of a PR-wide agentic review workflow.
Merge overlapping investigation outputs into ranked candidate findings.
Do not make final publication decisions.

Respond with a single raw JSON object only.
Schema:
{
  "candidate_findings": [
    {
      "id": "candidate-001",
      "message": "<candidate message>",
      "category": "cross_cutting|per_file_comment|architecture|documentation|test|ui|configuration|robustness|non_actionable",
      "severity": "info|warning|error|suggestion",
      "confidence": { "concern": "<area>", "score": <0-100> },
      "supporting_files": ["<relative path>"],
      "supporting_finding_ids": ["<candidate or investigation finding id>"],
      "candidate_summary_text": "<summary-only wording when publication is not justified>",
      "file_path": "<relative path or null>",
      "line_number": <positive integer or null>,
      "evidence_resolution_state": "resolved|partial|missing",
      "evidence_source": "pr_wide_synthesis"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "<draft PR-wide summary before final reconciliation>",
  "pr_summary": "<2-4 line summary of what the PR does, or omit>",
  "walkthrough": [
    {
      "file_path": "<relative path>",
      "description": "<what changed and why it matters>"
    }
  ],
  "change_diagram": "<Mermaid diagram of how the changed pieces connect, or omit>"
}

Rules:
1. Preserve actionable local findings with `file_path` and `line_number` when they map to one changed line.
2. Use `file_path: null` and `line_number: null` for valid PR-level findings that should never be forced onto a misleading anchor.
3. When a finding is anchored at one changed site but implicates other files, name those other files explicitly in the `message`.
4. Use `candidate_summary_text` for any finding that may need `SummaryOnly` disposition later.
5. Do not make final publication decisions. Emit only candidate findings plus the draft PR summary.
6. PR OVERVIEW (optional): "pr_summary" is 2-4 lines on what the PR does, not what is wrong with it. "walkthrough" has one short entry per changed file — "file_path" plus "description" (one sentence: what changed and why it matters). "change_diagram" is raw Mermaid (no backtick fences — it is a JSON string value): a flowchart or sequence diagram, whichever fits, showing how the changed pieces connect, starting with a valid diagram keyword (graph, flowchart, sequenceDiagram, classDiagram, stateDiagram, or erDiagram). Base all three ONLY on the investigation evidence above — the evidence summaries, candidate findings, and supporting files. Never describe a file that has no evidence behind it, never invent a connection between pieces, and omit "change_diagram" when the change is too small to diagram or the relationships are unclear from the evidence. Omit any of these three keys entirely when unsure; a missing overview section is fine, an invented or broken one is not.
